#@ readme_auth
A session cookie: `catalog-sync login {{name}} --form` posts `{{env_prefix}}_USER` /
`{{env_prefix}}_PASSWORD` (environment variables; the tool never reads a `.env` file) to the login
address in `credentials.py` and keeps the one cookie the answer sets (named in `credentials.py`), not
the whole jar. Every request then carries it as a `Cookie` header. A pasted cURL command cannot be
the source of a cookie: the parser drops cookies on purpose. A session cookie usually has no expiry
the tool can read, so `auth status` reports `unknown`; log in again when the service says 401.
